Description: EAP TLS 1.2 plus automatic Wi-Fi recovery
 Universal armv7 + arm64 build. Raises the TLS ceiling of the legacy
 iOS EAP client so WPA2-Enterprise networks such as ANU-Secure work.
 .
 Installs a launchd watchdog that recovers Wi-Fi when the device is
 associated but has no address, a self-assigned 169.254.x address, or no
 traffic (DHCP renew, then a clean wifid restart), and nudges auto-join
 when it stays unassociated. Log: /var/mobile/Media/wifi-watchdog.log
 .
 Supports rootful and rootless (/var/jb) jailbreaks and both the
 iOS 5/6 (kTLSProtocol1Only) and iOS 7+ (kTLSProtocol1) EAP contexts.
